    - target: {fileID: 3114651368704995631, guid: c67b0677017328ee1865993b2978d535,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Name
      value: Tutorial - Batteries
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6468995164157817124, guid: c67b0677017328ee1865993b2978d535,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: '- Batteries store power: they charge through their input side and release
        it through their output side...............................

        - A
        battery never passes power straight through. Everything after it gets no
        more than it can release......................

        - Power arriving
        at a full battery turns into heat..............................

        -
        A charged battery can keep things running while the reactor is off, and can
        power the reactor to start it'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6468995164157817124, guid: c67b0677017328ee1865993b2978d535,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontSize
      value: 0.55
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6468995164157817124, guid: c67b0677017328ee1865993b2978d535,
